1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,960
You're trying to get a crumpled bill into the gas station's payment machine when the

2
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:04,640
sky changes.

3
00:00:05,420 --> 00:00:09,780
You look for storm clouds, but the dark shape overhead has a perfectly straight edge.

4
00:00:10,340 --> 00:00:15,100
It slides across the evening sun, and every shadow on the forecourt disappears at once.

5
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:17,520
Your milk is still sitting beside the pump.

6
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:19,200
Your bag is by your feet.

7
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,120
Across the road, the traffic lights turn green in every direction.

8
00:00:24,020 --> 00:00:24,620
Nothing moves.

9
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:27,580
Then every car horn starts together.

10
00:00:27,580 --> 00:00:30,200
You grab the bag and run toward the shop.

11
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:32,540
Halfway there, you look up.

12
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:35,300
Something enormous hangs above the city.

13
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:39,600
Silent enough that you can hear the payment machine rejecting your bill.

14
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:43,380
A smaller shape separates from its underside.

15
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:50,240
It settles onto the road without wheels, without smoke, without anything you recognize as an engine.

16
00:00:51,260 --> 00:00:52,280
The shop door is open.

17
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:53,640
You go through it.

18
00:00:54,160 --> 00:00:56,480
Two figures step out of the smaller craft.

19
00:00:56,480 --> 00:00:58,760
Smooth pale green faces.

20
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:00,140
Black eyes.

21
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:04,280
Sealed dark uniforms that rise around their narrow necks.

22
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:07,860
One has a blue stripe across its shoulder.

23
00:01:08,620 --> 00:01:10,280
The other carries a flat metal case.

24
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:12,000
You almost laugh.

25
00:01:12,780 --> 00:01:17,120
Your brain has picked a strange time to insist that costumes can't look that good.

26
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:19,240
The striped one raises a scanner.

27
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:22,220
A pale line travels across the parked cars.

28
00:01:22,860 --> 00:01:24,460
Then through the space where you were standing.

29
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:26,360
You drop behind the counter.

30
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:28,640
The line crosses the shop window.

31
00:01:29,540 --> 00:01:32,300
A bottle slips from your bag and rolls toward the entrance.

32
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:34,500
It stops against the door.

33
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:36,380
The scanner stops too.

34
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:38,680
For six seconds, nothing happens.

35
00:01:39,740 --> 00:01:41,240
Then the striped figure turns away.

36
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:44,060
The other places a small marker on the pavement.

37
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:46,740
Two circles joined by a short line.

38
00:01:47,580 --> 00:01:49,400
You stay down until your knees hurt.

39
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:51,400
Your phone has no signal.

40
00:01:52,580 --> 00:01:53,440
Emergency calls fail.

41
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:59,960
The last message on the screen is a delivery notification for a package you're probably never going to receive.

42
00:02:00,820 --> 00:02:04,180
On the first night, your entire world shrinks to the shop.

43
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:08,160
You carry bottled water and packaged food into the staff room.

44
00:02:08,840 --> 00:02:11,520
You close the door and cover the windows with flattened cartons.

45
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:12,880
That feels important.

46
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,280
You leave the refrigerated food alone.

47
00:02:16,020 --> 00:02:17,540
You don't know when the power will fail.

48
00:02:18,060 --> 00:02:20,440
And you don't want tonight's dinner to become tomorrow's problem.

49
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:24,480
You find a flashlight, a pencil, and a roll of receipt paper.

50
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:27,620
On the back of a receipt, you write what you've seen.

51
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:31,920
Two figures, blue stripe, scanner, circles.

52
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:34,860
The notes look manageable on the little receipt.

53
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:37,080
You keep looking up at the window.

54
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:41,140
Before midnight, something scrapes across the forecourt.

55
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:44,280
You crouch at the shop's edge and look out.

56
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:47,440
The plain figure shifts an abandoned bicycle

57
00:02:47,440 --> 00:02:52,960
exactly one step away from the marker, leaves it there, and walks away.

58
00:02:53,740 --> 00:02:55,420
You don't understand the difference yet.

59
00:02:56,140 --> 00:02:57,800
Morning arrives on day two.

60
00:02:58,380 --> 00:02:59,460
The ship is still there.

61
00:03:00,020 --> 00:03:03,560
The station has water, food, a roof, and walls.

62
00:03:04,340 --> 00:03:10,740
Outside, you have a road full of motionless cars and no idea what happened to the people inside them.

63
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:12,180
Staying seems obvious.

64
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:13,680
You start an inventory.

65
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:19,240
Sealed drinks, tins, crackers, a few dozen snack packets.

66
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:21,600
Some things you can count immediately.

67
00:03:22,580 --> 00:03:26,680
Others are scattered across shelves you can't reach without standing in view of the windows.

68
00:03:27,520 --> 00:03:33,900
You give the unreachable shelves their own column, so you won't accidentally count them as supplies in the staff room.

69
00:03:34,580 --> 00:03:37,680
Six cases of bottled water are already behind the counter.

70
00:03:38,380 --> 00:03:39,980
Eighteen liters in each case.

71
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:42,720
You write down the total, then circle it.

72
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:48,520
There are 96 tins you can reach without crossing the shop, plus crackers and snack packets.

73
00:03:49,320 --> 00:03:50,420
You check the total again.

74
00:03:51,140 --> 00:03:53,680
An ordinary delivery would restock the shelves tomorrow.

75
00:03:54,380 --> 00:03:57,840
Now you need the cases to last without knowing when you can replace them.

76
00:03:58,620 --> 00:04:00,980
You separate damage packaging from intact food.

77
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:03,160
You check dates instead of guessing.

78
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,820
Some of the tins need a closer look before they go in the stack.

79
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:09,880
You leave room on the paper for whatever you find next.

80
00:04:09,880 --> 00:04:13,240
That empty space starts bothering you immediately.

81
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,860
At 917, the scanner crosses the glass again.

82
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:19,140
You hold your breath in the staff room.

83
00:04:19,700 --> 00:04:21,180
The pale line never reaches you.

84
00:04:21,620 --> 00:04:23,720
When it's gone, you write down the time.

85
00:04:24,540 --> 00:04:26,740
At 957, it comes back.

86
00:04:27,460 --> 00:04:28,000
40 minutes.

87
00:04:28,980 --> 00:04:32,380
You want that to be a rule so badly that you almost decide it's one.

88
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:35,980
In the afternoon, you hear the shop's little entrance bell.

89
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:37,560
Someone is coming in.

90
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:42,260
You lift your flashlight with both hands, which is not nearly as impressive as you hoped.

91
00:04:43,020 --> 00:04:44,200
A woman stops in the doorway.

92
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:49,140
She has a violet band around one forearm and a turquoise bag held by its handle.

93
00:04:49,740 --> 00:04:50,700
Her other hand is open.

94
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:52,440
She says her name is Mara.

95
00:04:53,220 --> 00:04:54,580
She says she saw you move yesterday.

96
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:58,860
That sentence makes you lower the flashlight less quickly than she would like.

97
00:04:59,380 --> 00:05:01,940
She has four sealed bottles and food from her bag.

98
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:04,580
She also has an observation you don't have.

99
00:05:04,580 --> 00:05:10,200
The striped figure scans the same stretch of road, but the plain one changes what is on it.

100
00:05:10,740 --> 00:05:12,800
She watched it move three things out of the road.

101
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:15,780
Then she watched it move a fourth thing into the road.

102
00:05:16,420 --> 00:05:17,680
An empty red fuel can.

103
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:20,060
You saw that can beside the pump yesterday.

104
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:22,560
Now it stands beside the two circles.

105
00:05:23,380 --> 00:05:24,140
You let Mara stay.

106
00:05:24,880 --> 00:05:27,220
You put her supplies into a separate column first.

107
00:05:27,960 --> 00:05:29,340
Neither of you comments on that.

108
00:05:29,820 --> 00:05:32,600
She notices you looking at her bag whenever she moves it.

109
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:35,560
Eventually she empties it in front of you.

110
00:05:36,020 --> 00:05:39,300
Food, bottles, a folded jacket, nothing else.

111
00:05:40,180 --> 00:05:41,840
You show her your supplies in return.

112
00:05:42,860 --> 00:05:46,660
You tell her how many bottles you've counted and she checks the total with you.

113
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:49,760
Before sleeping she asks what to call you.

114
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:51,340
Read you say.

115
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:55,220
For a moment saying your own name feels stranger than anything outside.

116
00:05:56,300 --> 00:05:58,500
Yesterday saying it was just an introduction.

117
00:05:59,540 --> 00:06:01,780
Mara repeats it to make sure she heard you.

118
00:06:01,780 --> 00:06:03,920
Then puts her bag beside the supplies.

119
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:08,020
By day three you have watched six complete patrols.

120
00:06:08,980 --> 00:06:13,480
The striped figure arrives, raises the scanner, and pauses at the joined circles.

121
00:06:14,660 --> 00:06:15,640
The plain figure follows.

122
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:17,980
Sometimes it carries something.

123
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:20,660
Sometimes it leaves with something.

124
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:22,160
Neither seems hurried.

125
00:06:23,140 --> 00:06:27,160
Between passes you and Mara move supplies into the staff room.

126
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:30,020
One watches, the other carries.

127
00:06:30,660 --> 00:06:32,220
You don't cross the forecourt.

128
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:36,780
You add three more water cases and another stack of tins to the inventory.

129
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:39,520
Those cases are now on your list.

130
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:42,820
You still haven't checked the shelves beside the front window.

131
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:46,940
You used to think of a place like this as somewhere that never ran out.

132
00:06:47,540 --> 00:06:52,260
You count each case you bring into the room and check how much space is left on the shelf.

133
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:54,580
You make marks on the receipt roll.

134
00:06:55,260 --> 00:06:55,840
Meals taken.

135
00:06:56,820 --> 00:06:57,340
Bottles opened.

136
00:06:58,500 --> 00:06:58,800
Patrol times.

137
00:06:59,540 --> 00:07:02,480
You keep the paper dry inside an empty tin.

138
00:07:03,340 --> 00:07:05,720
The longest line is the one headed unknown.

139
00:07:06,820 --> 00:07:09,100
On day five you test something small.

140
00:07:09,740 --> 00:07:13,740
Mara sets an empty carton beside the red can while you watch from the shop.

141
00:07:14,620 --> 00:07:18,960
It takes her less than a minute and both of you spend the next half hour regretting it.

142
00:07:19,640 --> 00:07:20,700
The plain figure returns.

143
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:23,320
It moves the carton behind the marker.

144
00:07:24,180 --> 00:07:25,580
It leaves the can where it is.

145
00:07:26,020 --> 00:07:27,020
You try to see a pattern.

146
00:07:27,020 --> 00:07:28,940
Maybe the road has to stay clear.

147
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:31,320
Maybe certain objects count as obstacles.

148
00:07:32,300 --> 00:07:34,900
Maybe the can means something neither of you can read.

149
00:07:35,640 --> 00:07:36,820
You don't test a second object.

150
00:07:37,580 --> 00:07:40,360
Instead, you remove the shop's entrance bell.

151
00:07:40,940 --> 00:07:43,820
It's the little mechanical kind that rings when the door moves.

152
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:46,380
You put it in a drawer wrapped in a cloth.

153
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:51,420
The next time Mara opens the door there is only the soft scrape of its bottom edge.

154
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:52,440
It helps.

155
00:07:53,040 --> 00:07:55,440
It also means you have removed your own warning.

156
00:07:55,980 --> 00:07:59,820
From now on, silence at the entrance can't tell you the shop is empty.

157
00:08:00,580 --> 00:08:03,380
That evening Mara asks where you would go if you had to leave.

158
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:05,320
You say away from the ship.

159
00:08:05,940 --> 00:08:09,160
She points out that the ship is above most of the places you can see.

160
00:08:09,940 --> 00:08:13,600
You draw the station, the roadside path, and the bend beyond it.

161
00:08:14,260 --> 00:08:15,160
The drawing is ugly.

162
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:18,220
For now, it's your entire escape plan.

163
00:08:19,020 --> 00:08:21,380
On day seven, the station loses power.

164
00:08:21,380 --> 00:08:24,880
The refrigerator hum ends in the middle of a sentence.

165
00:08:25,660 --> 00:08:28,300
Outside, the pump displays go black.

166
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:30,220
Your phone is already dead.

167
00:08:30,820 --> 00:08:32,680
Now the familiar noises are gone too.

168
00:08:33,420 --> 00:08:35,980
You move the bottled drinks out of the shop's colder cabinets

169
00:08:35,980 --> 00:08:39,920
and stop treating electricity as something that might come back tonight.

170
00:08:40,760 --> 00:08:42,500
There is a working tap for another day.

171
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:46,860
Then, there is a weak cough, a little water, and nothing.

172
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:49,020
You count the sealed drinks again.

173
00:08:49,020 --> 00:08:51,420
The number is smaller than it felt yesterday.

174
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:53,740
Food will last longer than the drinks.

175
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:57,440
You need to get more bottled water while you still have a way to reach it.

176
00:08:57,960 --> 00:09:02,580
The remaining shop stock would help, but some of it sits directly beside the front window.

177
00:09:03,520 --> 00:09:04,700
You watch the scanner pass.

178
00:09:05,380 --> 00:09:07,600
Forty minutes later, it passes again.

179
00:09:08,460 --> 00:09:11,440
You tell Mara that you can get the bottles after the next sweep.

180
00:09:12,060 --> 00:09:14,320
She asks whether the scanner is the only thing watching.

181
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:16,100
You have no answer.

182
00:09:16,820 --> 00:09:17,280
You go anyway.

183
00:09:17,280 --> 00:09:20,040
You bring the cases back one at a time.

184
00:09:20,660 --> 00:09:25,020
On the fourth trip, the receipt you tucked into your pocket catches on the shelf and falls.

185
00:09:25,860 --> 00:09:26,260
You leave it.

186
00:09:27,160 --> 00:09:29,940
One sheet of paper is not worth another crossing.

187
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:35,380
When the patrol returns, the striped figure stops inside the shop for the first time.

188
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:37,320
Its scanner points down.

189
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:38,700
Toward your receipt.

190
00:09:39,760 --> 00:09:42,500
By day ten, the red can has moved again.

191
00:09:43,280 --> 00:09:45,900
It now sits beside the mouth of the roadside path.

192
00:09:45,900 --> 00:09:49,240
A second joined circle marker has appeared beside it.

193
00:09:49,820 --> 00:09:52,000
The aliens have not broken the station windows.

194
00:09:52,740 --> 00:09:54,380
They haven't forced the staff room door.

195
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:57,400
You tell yourself that a closed room keeps you safe.

196
00:09:58,180 --> 00:09:59,240
You have evidence for that.

197
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:00,800
Several days of it.

198
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:04,260
Mara asks what you'll do if the scanner changes again.

199
00:10:05,020 --> 00:10:08,520
She wants to follow the path before it becomes another place you can't use.

200
00:10:09,260 --> 00:10:10,960
You want one more night to plan.

201
00:10:11,700 --> 00:10:13,620
You compromise on watching it from the yard.

202
00:10:13,620 --> 00:10:16,500
At dusk, the plane figure walks to the bend.

203
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:18,900
It puts its metal case on the ground.

204
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:23,700
A thin light rises out of it, hangs there for a moment, and goes out.

205
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:26,580
The striped figure stays by the station.

206
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:30,480
For the first time, you can't see both of them from one place.

207
00:10:31,100 --> 00:10:33,960
You stop writing 40 minutes on the receipt as if it's a guarantee.

208
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:36,600
You write observed beside it instead.

209
00:10:37,580 --> 00:10:40,400
On day twelve, your closed room stops being safe.

210
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:44,260
Your sorting food when a pale stripe crosses the inside wall.

211
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:48,060
The door is shut, but the stripe shines through the solid wall.

212
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:52,840
It passes across the shelf, over Mara's empty bag, and down to the floor.

213
00:10:53,580 --> 00:10:55,320
Then it returns to the bag and waits.

214
00:10:56,300 --> 00:10:57,780
You flatten yourself behind the supplies.

215
00:10:58,620 --> 00:11:00,240
Mara does the same on the other side.

216
00:11:00,820 --> 00:11:02,320
Neither of you moves toward the door.

217
00:11:03,060 --> 00:11:03,660
The stripe disappears.

218
00:11:04,380 --> 00:11:08,680
Outside, the plane figure makes a short scraping sound against the building.

219
00:11:08,680 --> 00:11:13,300
When the patrol leaves, you find a joined circle mark at the base of the wall.

220
00:11:14,020 --> 00:11:15,560
Your shelter is on their map now.

221
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:18,040
You don't know whether the scanner saw you.

222
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:20,540
You know it can reach farther than you thought.

223
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:25,820
You move into the yard's sheltered corner for the next pass, taking only what you can carry.

224
00:11:26,680 --> 00:11:28,660
The scanner pauses at the staff room again.

225
00:11:29,280 --> 00:11:31,180
It seems to be checking where you used to be.

226
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:33,280
The empty room might buy you time.

227
00:11:33,780 --> 00:11:37,000
You keep listening to see whether the scanner is moving toward the yard.

228
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:40,020
Mara wants to retrieve the rest of her things immediately.

229
00:11:40,840 --> 00:11:42,800
You ask her to wait until the patrol is gone.

230
00:11:43,460 --> 00:11:46,100
The delay leaves you both outside as the evening gets colder.

231
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:49,900
She doesn't complain, but you see her looking toward the jacket inside.

232
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:51,920
Your hands are getting cold too.

233
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:54,580
You keep them tucked under your arms and wait.

234
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:59,180
By day 15, you have two sleeping places and no good night sleep.

235
00:11:59,980 --> 00:12:02,260
You move between them without keeping the same hours.

236
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:06,980
You eat sitting down with the food on your knees, so you can pick it up quick.

237
00:12:07,780 --> 00:12:12,460
Before you move again, you check that you can carry everything without making a second trip.

238
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:17,140
You shift the spare water case closer to the yard, lifting it with both hands.

239
00:12:17,680 --> 00:12:21,200
Outside, you can see the empty red can sitting by the path.

240
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:24,340
You keep checking whether the aliens have moved it again.

241
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:27,200
The aliens move it to the far side of the path.

242
00:12:27,880 --> 00:12:29,360
Then they leave it there for three days.

243
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:31,220
Mara thinks it marks a boundary.

244
00:12:32,040 --> 00:12:33,960
You think it marks something they expect to return.

245
00:12:34,480 --> 00:12:37,160
Neither theory makes walking past it feel better.

246
00:12:37,880 --> 00:12:38,820
You argue about leaving.

247
00:12:39,580 --> 00:12:42,060
It's a quiet argument which somehow makes it worse.

248
00:12:42,900 --> 00:12:44,860
She says the station is becoming a trap.

249
00:12:45,640 --> 00:12:49,740
You say the station is the only place where you understand even part of the danger.

250
00:12:50,220 --> 00:12:52,780
Later, you find that she has packed her bag.

251
00:12:53,460 --> 00:12:55,680
She has left your pencil beside the receipt tin.

252
00:12:56,420 --> 00:13:00,560
You glance at her packed bag, then check the route on the map again while she waits.

253
00:13:01,140 --> 00:13:04,720
On day 18, you go as far as the bend together.

254
00:13:05,740 --> 00:13:07,560
The road beyond is not empty.

255
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:10,520
Dark shapes stand at intervals along it.

256
00:13:11,020 --> 00:13:13,480
Each has the same joint circles near its base.

257
00:13:14,260 --> 00:13:16,740
You can't see far enough to tell where the line ends.

258
00:13:17,540 --> 00:13:21,920
The route out of the city is being organized, but you don't know what it leads to.

259
00:13:22,520 --> 00:13:26,000
Whatever these units are setting up, they keep working on it.

260
00:13:26,440 --> 00:13:29,560
You watch one return to the same mark spot before you head back.

261
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:34,440
You stay beside Mara at the bend, keeping low enough that the units can't see you.

262
00:13:34,840 --> 00:13:37,920
You leave a small crease on the edge of your paper map where you stopped.

263
00:13:38,660 --> 00:13:43,260
Mara asks whether that's the farthest you can go or simply the farthest you have gone.

264
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:44,920
You say you don't know.

265
00:13:45,640 --> 00:13:47,020
The conversation stops there.

266
00:13:47,480 --> 00:13:50,200
You both watch the bend until it's time to turn back.

267
00:13:50,920 --> 00:13:54,160
On the way back, you agree that the next trip must change something.

268
00:13:54,160 --> 00:13:58,600
More distance, a new view, a reason to accept the risk.

269
00:13:59,140 --> 00:14:02,460
Otherwise, you're only repeating the same frightened walk.

270
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:06,060
At the station, the plane figure is inside the shop.

271
00:14:06,700 --> 00:14:09,900
You crouch outside and watch it gather the loose cartons from the floor.

272
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:12,680
It lays them beside the shelf in a neat row.

273
00:14:13,340 --> 00:14:15,560
Then it finds the gap where you took the water cases.

274
00:14:16,400 --> 00:14:18,620
It touches that gap with one gloved hand.

275
00:14:19,260 --> 00:14:23,880
When it leaves, you find a vertical line with a short stroke across it below the shelf.

276
00:14:23,880 --> 00:14:26,900
You compare it with the joined circles on your receipt.

277
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:29,780
Your stock has become another thing they're measuring.

278
00:14:30,540 --> 00:14:33,520
You open the tin and add a sentence to the receipt roll.

279
00:14:34,140 --> 00:14:35,140
They notice what changes.

280
00:14:36,140 --> 00:14:38,440
On day 21, the patrol comes early.

281
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:42,740
You're returning from the yard with Mara when the scanner lights the shop window.

282
00:14:43,540 --> 00:14:45,640
You haven't even reached your usual hiding place.

283
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:48,240
You stop behind a stack of stored crates.

284
00:14:49,140 --> 00:14:50,320
Mara stops beside you.

285
00:14:50,320 --> 00:14:53,420
The supplies in your hands feel suddenly enormous.

286
00:14:54,420 --> 00:14:56,340
The striped figure walks past the window.

287
00:14:57,000 --> 00:15:00,320
You can see the blue shoulder stripe through a gap between two crates.

288
00:15:01,240 --> 00:15:02,700
Then the pale line turns.

289
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:06,120
It searches the space you used after the last surprise.

290
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:09,940
You can't use either of your regular hiding places now.

291
00:15:10,620 --> 00:15:13,040
The scanner is moving through both of them while you're outside.

292
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:16,080
You lower the supplies without dropping them.

293
00:15:16,660 --> 00:15:20,280
Mara presses her hand against the crate as it begins to shift.

294
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:24,200
For a moment, the entire stack leans toward the open yard.

295
00:15:24,740 --> 00:15:25,020
It settles.

296
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:26,900
The patrol continues.

297
00:15:27,620 --> 00:15:31,400
Afterward, you find that one water bottle has split beneath the case.

298
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:32,640
The floor is wet.

299
00:15:33,380 --> 00:15:37,140
You try to save what remains sealed and you cross another bottle off the ledger.

300
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:40,380
Mara holds the split bottle above the wet floor.

301
00:15:41,180 --> 00:15:43,920
You set it aside and count the intact ones again.

302
00:15:43,920 --> 00:15:49,180
By day 24, you expect to find the aliens inside the shop every time you return.

303
00:15:50,040 --> 00:15:52,360
You watch the entrance before bringing anything in.

304
00:15:53,020 --> 00:15:54,680
The aliens still have not attacked.

305
00:15:55,300 --> 00:15:56,500
That used to comfort you.

306
00:15:57,080 --> 00:15:58,920
Now their patience is what keeps you awake.

307
00:15:59,900 --> 00:16:01,880
On your receipt, the bottle count keeps falling.

308
00:16:02,620 --> 00:16:05,220
The workers return with their case while you finish counting.

309
00:16:06,020 --> 00:16:07,860
You and Mara search the shelves once more.

310
00:16:08,700 --> 00:16:08,980
Food remains.

311
00:16:10,980 --> 00:16:12,460
Sealed water is harder to find.

312
00:16:12,460 --> 00:16:15,080
You collect what is left and make two piles.

313
00:16:15,860 --> 00:16:16,380
What you carry.

314
00:16:17,140 --> 00:16:17,680
What stays.

315
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:21,420
You leave the heavy things that do not help you tomorrow.

316
00:16:22,360 --> 00:16:24,340
The ledger is longer than your arm now.

317
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:27,300
Mara reads the first entries then the last.

318
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:28,700
40 minutes.

319
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:29,980
Closed room.

320
00:16:30,660 --> 00:16:31,800
Safe behind the wall.

321
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:33,620
You don't cross those lines out.

322
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:36,260
You need to remember how convincing they looked.

323
00:16:37,140 --> 00:16:38,780
Together, you mark what you know today.

324
00:16:39,460 --> 00:16:40,240
The scanner changes.

325
00:16:40,240 --> 00:16:42,660
The workers track disturbed places.

326
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:44,700
The road marks are spreading.

327
00:16:45,260 --> 00:16:48,060
None of those statements says what will happen if you're caught.

328
00:16:48,680 --> 00:16:49,960
You fold the map into the tin.

329
00:16:50,460 --> 00:16:51,720
The lid no longer fits neatly.

330
00:16:52,540 --> 00:16:56,120
On day 27, the plane figure stops clearing the forecourt.

331
00:16:56,780 --> 00:16:59,800
Instead, it moves the red can back beneath the canopy.

332
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:02,260
It places its case beside a pump.

333
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:05,820
The striped figure scans the building from top to bottom.

334
00:17:06,220 --> 00:17:09,760
When they leave, a narrow band of pale light stays on the ground.

335
00:17:09,760 --> 00:17:11,560
Circling the entire station.

336
00:17:12,380 --> 00:17:13,680
You haven't seen that before.

337
00:17:14,460 --> 00:17:17,500
The band crosses the path you use between the shop and the yard.

338
00:17:17,980 --> 00:17:19,020
You watch for an hour.

339
00:17:19,540 --> 00:17:20,180
It never fades.

340
00:17:21,020 --> 00:17:23,160
Mara points to the arrows on your first sketch.

341
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:25,420
Each route crosses the new light.

342
00:17:26,100 --> 00:17:29,160
She follows one arrow with her finger and stops at the line.

343
00:17:29,640 --> 00:17:32,520
That night, you move the bags close to the root out.

344
00:17:33,080 --> 00:17:34,400
You don't step across the light.

345
00:17:34,820 --> 00:17:37,640
You don't have enough knowledge to turn yourself into another test.

346
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:39,920
You wait for something else to cross.

347
00:17:40,480 --> 00:17:41,040
Nothing does.

348
00:17:41,740 --> 00:17:43,500
Day 30 arrives without an alarm.

349
00:17:44,020 --> 00:17:45,100
You wake to scraping metal.

350
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:47,280
Both aliens are working at the pumps.

351
00:17:47,920 --> 00:17:51,420
A line runs from their case toward the small craft waiting on the road.

352
00:17:52,080 --> 00:17:54,720
The red can sits at the center of the glowing boundary.

353
00:17:55,560 --> 00:17:57,340
Then the shop shelves begin to vibrate.

354
00:17:57,940 --> 00:17:59,740
A tin walks slowly toward the edge.

355
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:01,680
You catch it before it falls.

356
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:04,040
Outside the canopy shivers.

357
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:07,120
A thin crack opens along the shop window.

358
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:10,640
The crack spreads farther down the glass while you watch.

359
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:12,680
You have food for the journey.

360
00:18:13,540 --> 00:18:16,000
You have the last sealed drinks you could find.

361
00:18:16,600 --> 00:18:22,960
You have one flashlight with a fading beam and a map of a road you have never followed beyond the bend.

362
00:18:23,620 --> 00:18:26,100
You don't have another safe night at this station.

363
00:18:26,900 --> 00:18:28,120
Mara picks up her bag.

364
00:18:28,820 --> 00:18:29,540
You pick up yours.

365
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:31,940
The receipt tin goes with you.

366
00:18:31,940 --> 00:18:37,080
30 days of being wrong might still help you get the next decision right.

367
00:18:37,780 --> 00:18:41,840
Through the cracked window, you see the striped figure turn toward the shop.

368
00:18:42,720 --> 00:18:45,120
The pale boundary opens at the roadside path.

369
00:18:46,080 --> 00:18:46,340
One gap.

370
00:18:47,220 --> 00:18:48,740
Wide enough for two people to leave.

371
00:18:49,780 --> 00:18:54,560
Beyond it, the joint circle markers light up one after another, leading toward the bend.

372
00:18:55,740 --> 00:18:56,620
Mara looks at the opening.

373
00:18:57,460 --> 00:18:58,480
Then she looks at you.

374
00:18:58,480 --> 00:19:01,820
The aliens have finally given you a way out.

375
00:19:02,300 --> 00:19:05,100
You have no idea where they expect you to go.
